PROVISIONAL (proposed to Guillaume Duboc; replace it with his fix when there is one).
Tallying did not terminate on a recursive solution whose variable occurs in a Boolean
combination below a constructor, such as {x or :b} <= x: the solution is a node whose
generator substitutes the node for x, and computing x or :b unfolds the node, which
runs the generator again. In structural mode, such elements are substituted lazily, in
nodes of their own; the copies made by substitute_recursive_node/4 are named after the
substitution, and the lazy nodes after the element and the substitution, so that the
same unfolding gives the same nodes; structural substitution does not simplify; and
the polymorphic leaves that connectives store when they unfold a node are exposed, also
in emptiness checks.

